77fa|n|See Plow. ; A well-known implement, drawn by horses, mules, oxen, or other power, for turning up the soil to prepare it for bearing crops; also used to furrow or break up the soil for other purposes; as, the subsoil plow; the draining plow. ; Fig.: Agriculture; husbandry. ; A carucate of land; a plowland. ; A joiner's plane for making grooves; a grooving plane. ; An implement for trimming or shaving off the edges of books. ; Same as Charles's Wain. ; To cut a groove in, as in a plank, or the edge of a board; especially, a rectangular groove to receive the end of a shelf or tread, the edge of a panel, a tongue, etc.	a:8t59,63,3;40z7,62,10;6tfq,8,3~40z7,62,10;6tfq,8,3;8t59,63,3	v:aivj,113,4;9bbt,55,3~aivj,113,4;9bbt,55,3	V:3sf5,27,5;944x,20,1;a6ev,2,5~3sf5,27,5;a6ev,2,5;944x,20,1	n:9bbt,39,1~9bbt,39,1	N:aqnf,79,3;12i1,43,1;al51,24,7~al51,24,7;aqnf,79,3;12i1,43,1
